virglrenderer: Venus proc table entries are never NULL

What: when vkr loads a physical device's or a device's proc table, every entry
the driver did not give gets a stub of the entry's own type
(vkr_missing_entries.c, from the generated list vkr_proc_entries.h): a command of
a Vulkan version or extension the app's instance or device was not made with.
Called while a thread dispatches an app's commands (vkr_context_submit_cmd or a
ring thread set the per-thread vkr_dispatching_context), a stub ends that app's
Venus context with a log line; called from vkr's own code (a blob export, the
context's end) it logs and returns an error, so the caller fails. The
physical-device queries of four device extensions (calibrated timestamps,
cooperative matrix, fragment shading rate, sample locations) count only when the
device lists the extension: the Vulkan loader gives an entry for each and ends
the process when the driver lacks it. Entries are never NULL from here on:
VKR_MISSING tells a stub, and the six checks that tested NULL use it (#623's four
device-image queries, which answer zeros, and the two Metal handle calls). A
static assert stops the build when upstream adds an entry, until
vkr_proc_entries.h is made again (Tests/virgl/venus-missing-entries.py).
Why: a device's entries follow MIN(the driver's version, the guest's instance
apiVersion) and its extensions: on a 1.1 device without extensions 148 of 286
are NULL on KosmicKrisp (146 on MoltenVK), and 130 guest commands call such an
entry without a check. A guest program sending one (vkCmdSetCullMode on a 1.1
device, any acceleration structure command, vkQueueSubmit2 ...) made QEMU call
address 0, on every path (command buffer, generated create, query, queue, the
MESA commands, a ring thread, nested streams) and on KosmicKrisp and MoltenVK
(M4, macOS 27, one process per case, 3 runs). A stub at load covers every dispatch function and vkr's own calls and
costs nothing per command; a lookup in the dispatch layer would need a hand-kept
map of commands to entries and would miss vkr's own calls.
Upstream: a vkr bug on every host (a guest can send any command); draft in
work/upstream-drafts/virglrenderer-venus-missing-entries.md, not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-venus-robust.c (build time): after a 1.1 device without
extensions every entry is set and the stubs are the missing ones; the n- and p-
cases end the process before the patch and only the context after it; #623's
queries on such a device still answer zeros; a stub vkr calls itself returns an
error; vkr_context_submit_cmd puts the dispatching context back.
run-venus-limits.py checks vkr_proc_entries.h against the built tree.

